  "description": "A re-entry with OPTIONI '05', which reaches the second term of the guard at app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl:128, WS-OPTION > CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT. app/cpy/COADM02Y.cpy:20 declares that count as 4, so 5 is one past the last valued entry - and it is rejected even though CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT is declared OCCURS 9, which is exactly the point: the count and not the table size bounds the subscript, so line 143 can never address slot 5, whose bytes lie past the group COADM02Y actually gives values to. The option is numeric and non-zero, so this is the one guard term the other two rejections cannot reach.",
